# Setup Doctor

DNS diagnosis (SPF/DKIM/DMARC/MX). Findings come from deterministic checks only. The LLM rewrites; `verify_plan` / grounding rejects inventions; fallback is the template.

```
check → explain → verify → render
 ↘ fallback → render
```

Packages (see `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`):

- `core/` — Finding, DiagnosisResult, observability
- `dns/` — Resolver, SPF parse
- `checks/` — registry + engine (Findings only)
- `explain/` — template/LLM + verify + report
- `pipeline/` — diagnose graph
- `integrations/` — Instantly, reputation (signals / unknown)
- `surfaces/` — CLI, API, MCP (thin; no parallel DNS logic)

## Rules

- Never weaken tests, fixture labels, or mutants to get green.
- New checks need: labeled fixture (incl. boundary), unit test under `tests/checks/`, mutant in `evals/mutations/mutation_check.py`; register in `checks/registry.py`.
- Model output must not create, remove, or re-rank findings.
- Surfaces/skills call `diagnose` / `diagnose_result` — no SPF/DKIM logic in Markdown skills.
- Outage ≠ absence (`ResolverError` vs empty records).
- No fabricated metrics or API shapes — Instantly/reputation missing ⇒ unknown / not_checked.
- After changes: run `pytest`, `evals/run_evals.py`, `evals/mutation_check.py`; keep README / `evals/RESULTS.md` numbers honest. Shadow never inflates synthetic P/R.
- Secrets only via env; never print keys.
- Python 3.10+, type hints; no new deps without a reason.
- Keep dependency direction: surfaces → pipeline → checks/explain → dns/core.
